{"content":[{"c":["CITY OF DAVID"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Southeastern hill (Ophel) in the present-day city of Jerusalem, the site occupied by King David as his royal city; also called Zion (e.g., ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.8.1","r":"1Kgs.8.1","rawR":"1Kgs.8.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.8.1","value":"1Kgs.8.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 8:1"},"). David captured the Jebusite fortress of Jerusalem and transferred his capital to it from Hebron (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.5.1-10","r":"2Sam.5.1-10","rawR":"2Sam.5.1-10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.5.1-10","value":"2Sam.5.1-10"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 5:1-10"},"). ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Jerusalem_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Jerusalem_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Jerusalem_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Jerusalem"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Alternate name for Bethlehem, David’s hometown, in the NT (",{"href":"?bref=Luke.2.11","r":"Luke.2.11","rawR":"Luke.2.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.2.11","value":"Luke.2.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 2:11"},"). ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Bethlehem_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Bethlehem_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Bethlehem_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Bethlehem"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"CityofDavid","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 8:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.8.1","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.8.1","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.8.1"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 5:1-10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.5.1-10","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.5.1-10","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.5.1-10"},{"anchorText":"Lk 2:11","canonicalization":"defer